{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794385350635,"sessionID":"ses_e3651ea06ffejCbwMEiK3BtEML","part":{"id":"prt_1c9b38fd3001vxsMOYBsCZ9GVZ","messageID":"msg_1c9b375b2001ILufLdWcTRDS6t","sessionID":"ses_e3651ea06ffejCbwMEiK3BtEML","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794385350636,"sessionID":"ses_e3651ea06ffejCbwMEiK3BtEML","part":{"id":"prt_1c9b38fd6001e5CjqovuxQHhfF","messageID":"msg_1c9b375b2001ILufLdWcTRDS6t","sessionID":"ses_e3651ea06ffejCbwMEiK3BtEML","type":"text","text":"This lock file with hashes triggers `--require-hashes` mode and fails in a clean install because transitive deps like `click>=8.1.3` aren't pinned with `==` (a known pip behavior). The README says the lock \"holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file.\"\n\nThe cleanest fix that keeps pinned/reproducible installs is to convert `requirements.lock` to a plain constraints file with pinned versions and no hashes. Since I only use stdlib Flask/Werkzeug/gunicorn and no new backend deps, I can regenerate it without hashes. Let me confirm a clean install works with the plain pinned constraints.","time":{"start":1794385350614,"end":1794385350632}}}
